  "scope": "Complete supported task namespace membership: unshare/setns/close_range, original Files/fs ownership, publication and all captured consumers.",
  "implementation": [
    "Original per-task bindings commit on the source; original mount contention parks the caller and retains the accepted namespace across FD close/reuse. Owner collection/custody imports bindings without replay.",
    "Files holds complete synchronized cold-control OFDs; ordinary Shared I/O is unchanged. Fs membership counts actual tasks and retires before cold projection collection.",
    "Future direct/native/async consumers refresh together; accepted async work keeps original descriptors, paths, execution context and wake target. Original actor roots are preserved.",
    "No new coordinator/resource thread, polling bus, per-call version check or ordinary guest-memory barrier. Serial execution avoids redundant candidate copies; private close_range/non-mount setns avoid unnecessary staging."
  ],
